{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". Count sequences of length n over {0,1} with no run of 3 same bits. Classic recurrence: Let a_n be number of strings length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit? We can use DP with states: last run length and last bit. But easier: Let A_n be number of strings length n ending with 0, with last run length 1; B_n ending with 0, run length 2; C_n ending with 1, run length 1; D_n ending with 1, run length 2. Recurrence: For n=1: A1=1 (0), B1=0, C1=1 (1), D1=0. For n>1: A_n = C_{n-1} + D_{n-1} (since to end with 0 run length1, previous must end with 1 run length1 or 2). B_n = A_{n-1} (since to end with 0 run length2, previous must end with 0 run length1). Similarly C_n = A_{n-1} + B_{n-1}. D_n = C_{n-1}. Total T_n = A_n+B_n+C_n+D_n.\n\nWe can compute quickly. Let's do iterative.\n\nn=1: A=1,B=0,C=1,D=0,T=2.\n\nn=2:\nA2 = C1 + D1 =1+0=1\nB2 = A1=1\nC2 = A1 + B1 =1+0=1\nD2 = C1=1\nT2=1+1+1+1=4\n\nn=3:\nA3 = C2 + D2 =1+1=2\nB3 = A2=1\nC3 = A2 + B2 =1+1=2\nD3 = C2=1\nT3=2+1+2+1=6\n\nn=4:\nA4 = C3 + D3 =2+1=3\nB4 = A3=2\nC4 = A3 + B3 =2+1=3\nD4 = C3=2\nT4=3+2+3+2=10\n\nn=5:\nA5 = C4 + D4 =3+2=5\nB5 = A4=3\nC5 = A4 + B4 =3+2=5\nD5 = C4=3\nT5=5+3+5+3=16\n\nn=6:\nA6 = C5 + D5 =5+3=8\nB6 = A5=5\nC6 = A5 + B5 =5+3=8\nD6 = C5=5\nT6=8+5+8+5=26\n\nn=7:\nA7 = C6 + D6 =8+5=13\nB7 = A6=8\nC7 = A6 + B6 =8+5=13\nD7 = C6=8\nT7=13+8+13+8=42\n\nn=8:\nA8 = C7 + D7 =13+8=21\nB8 = A7=13\nC8 = A7 + B7 =13+8=21\nD8 = C7=13\nT8=21+13+21+13=68\n\nn=9:\nA9 = C8 + D8"}}],"created":1790961109,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3713,"total_tokens":4481,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"c